    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="1275" n="1125" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1125"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Venezuelan Chargé to the Acting Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Venezuelan Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of your obliging note of the 5th instant, relative to the Peace
                    Conference and the steps taken with respect to its meeting.</p>
                <p>It affords me pleasure at the same time to inform you that I have been instructed
                    to advise the ambassador of Russia that my Government has directly addressed the
                    Netherlands Government and given it notice of the adhesion of Venezuela to the
                    second and third conventions of 1899, further declaring its decision to adhere
                    to the first as soon as it receives by telegraph notice of the assent of all the
                    powers which took part in the First Conference.</p>
                <p>Tendering you my best thanks for the information contained in your letter above
                    referred to, I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Garbiras
                    Guzman</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
